I’m debating with Chris whether you could use a costDF for asymmetric space use to achieve the same result as having a spatially varying sigma. Would be a cool vignette (or paper!) to do a comparison with some simulated data.

Murray and others have shown that compensation between p0 and sigma is quite robust to accommodating potentially misspecified variation. Should be easy to show with a simulation.

Right now oSCR cannot accommodate spatial variation in sigma, but that could be something worth developing.

